---
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/Base.astro";

const meta = {
	description:
		"Syed AbuTalib — software engineer on Chromium's audio stack at Google. Notes, posts, and browser media test pages.",
	title: "About",
};
---

<PageLayout meta={meta}>
	<h1 class="title mb-12">About</h1>
	<div class="prose prose-sm prose-cactus max-w-none">
		<p>
			Howdy, I'm Syed. I'm a software engineer at Google in Seattle, working on audio in Chromium,
			going from the <code>&lt;audio&gt;</code> tag all the way to your speakers.
		</p>
		<p>Some things I've worked on lately:</p>
		<ul class="list-inside list-disc" role="list">
			<li>
				Shipping IAMF (immersive / spatial audio) decoding in Chrome 153: the C++ streaming decoder,
				the design doc, and the Blink intent-to-ship.
			</li>
			<li>
				Reworking Chromium's multiprocess audio pipeline and its Mojo IPCs so it can carry 7.1.4 and
				5.1.4 layouts instead of stopping at 7.1.
			</li>
			<li>
				Fuzzing the audio stack with LibFuzzer and ClusterFuzz, which turned up 20+ memory-safety
				bugs in AOMedia's IAMF decoder. Also found a ten-year-old integer overflow in{" "}
				<code>base::CheckedNumeric</code>.
			</li>
			<li>
				Wiring up AVFoundation audio for Chrome on macOS, and reporting the bugs I find to Apple.
			</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			Before Chrome I spent two years on Google Cloud Marketplace's commerce backends (Java, gRPC,
			Spanner), and before that I built tools for the Private Investments team at Liberty Mutual in
			Boston (Django, React). I studied computer science at UT Dallas.
		</p>

		<h2>This site</h2>
		<p>
			Mostly <a href="/notes/">notes</a>: short TILs from work on codecs, containers, and browser
			media APIs. Occasionally a longer <a href="/posts/">post</a>. The <a href="/demos/">demos</a>{" "}
			are the test pages I use to poke at Media Source Extensions, WebCodecs, Web Audio, and
			multichannel playback. Feel free to use them.
		</p>

		<h2>Elsewhere</h2>
		<p>
			<a href="https://github.com/SyedAbuTalib" rel="noreferrer" target="_blank">
				GitHub
			</a>
			,{" "}
			<a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/syed-abutalib/" rel="noreferrer" target="_blank">
				LinkedIn
			</a>
			, or <a href="mailto:blog@jellyward.com">email</a>. There's also a{" "}
			<a href="/resume.pdf" rel="noreferrer" target="_blank">
				resume
			</a>{" "}
			if you want the formal version.
		</p>
	</div>
</PageLayout>
